@startuml Project01_ObjectDiagram
title Example agent instances (one simulated moment)

object "butterfly_101 : butterfly" as b1 {
  color = black
}

object "butterfly_102 : butterfly" as b2 {
  color = white
}

object "butterfly_103 : butterfly" as b3 {
  color = gray
}

object "predator_7 : predator" as p1

object "patch (left side) : patch_env" as patchA {
  background = black
}

object "patch (middle) : patch_env" as patchC {
  background = gray
}

object "patch (right side) : patch_env" as patchB {
  background = white
}

b1 -- patchA : standing on a matching\nblack patch — well hidden
b3 -- patchC : standing on a matching\ngray patch — well hidden
b2 -- patchB : standing on a matching\nwhite patch — well hidden

p1 ..> b3 : chasing this butterfly,\nbut it blends in well\nso it's hard to catch

note bottom
  This snapshot shows why camouflage matters: each butterfly
  happens to be standing on a patch close to its own color,
  making it harder for the predator to spot and catch them.
end note

@enduml
